'''''Murder Mystery 2''''', often abbreviated as "'''''MM2'''''”, is a popular Roblox experience created by [[Nikilis]] on January 18th, 2014 (however it did not become Murder Mystery 2 until December 25, 2014) as a successor to the original [[Murder Mystery|''Murder Mystery'']]. It is a round-based survival-type game with numerous different [[:Category:Maps|maps]] and [[Gamemodes|modes]]. It was heavily inspired by [https://gmod.fandom.com/wiki/Murder#:~:text=Garry's%20Mod%20%2D%20Murder%20is%20a,before%20it%20is%20too%20late. Garry's Mod: Murder] mode.

Players can level up, [[prestige]], and gain virtual [[:Category:Weapons|weapons]] (or variants of a weapon) from gambling on [[Boxes|mystery boxes]] or other means such as [[trading]] and [[crafting]].

<u>Over time, Murder Mystery 2 amassed over 30,000,000,000 visits. (as of September 2026)</u>

==Gameplay==
===<u>Loading Screen</u>===
[[File:7 Loading Screen Stages.png|thumb|All 7 Loading Screen Stages.]]
The Loading Screen is one of the most basic yet important features in Murder Mystery 2. Upon joining, players are immediately greeted with a Loading Screen, which ensures the game is fully rendered before gameplay commences. Murder Mystery 2 has always had a Loading Screen. Sometimes, loading is not successful. The duration and number of stages differ among individuals.

===<u>Game Modes</u>===
{{Dedicated Page|Link=[[Gamemodes]]}}
[[File:GamemodeSelectNEW.png|thumb|320x320px|The gamemode browser GUI.]]
{{See also|List of Links=[[Standard]], [[Disguises]], [[Assassin]]}}

[[File:Gamemode Select.png|thumb|220x220px|The Old gamemode select GUI.|alt=]]
Gamemodes, also known as "Modes,” are an optional way to play the game. As of now, there are three different game modes, those being Standard, Disguises, and Assassin. These modes can be switched by the player at any given time, and all the player’s data will be transferred. All game modes have their own separate place, but are still part of Murder Mystery 2.

====Standard====
Standard is the predetermined gamemode upon joining Murder Mystery 2. It features the four roles, which are the [[Innocent|Innocents]], the [[Sheriff]], the [[Hero]], and the [[Murderer]]. Players are allowed to zoom in and out, play as their own character, and use [[Powers]], [[Radios]], [[Pet Box|Pets]], and [[Emotes]].

====Disguises====
Disguises generally has the same basic mechanics as Standard. The core difference is that players are disguised by receiving different names based off of the NATO Phonetic Alphabet during rounds. Players’ avatars during rounds are also altered to appear similar to ensure that nobody knows who is who. [[Radios]] and [[Pets]] are not allowed. 

====Assassin====
Unlike Standard and Disguises where all four roles are implemented during rounds, Assassin only includes the [[Murderer]] role. All players upon the beginning of a round where everyone obtains a knife, and a screen of their target appears above. They must kill their target and avoid being killed. Like Standard, players are allowed to zoom in and out, play as their own character, and use [[Radios]], [[Emotes]], and [[Pets]]. However, [[Powers]] are not allowed to be used in Assassin unlike the other two game modes.

====Hardcore (removed/replaced)====
Hardcore was removed and replaced with the Disguises mode, and otherwise functions the same as Disguises mode, except the player was locked in first person mode.

===<u>Roles</u>===
{{Dedicated Page|Link=[[Roles]]}}

{{See also|List of Links=[[Innocent]], [[Sheriff]], [[Murderer]], [[Hero]]}}

Roles are given to players upon entering a round in Standard or Disguises [[Gamemodes|mode]] (with the exception of [[Hero]]), along with a percentage indicating how likely it is to be [[Murderer]]. The [[Innocent]] role can be given to a maximum of ten players, one player is given the [[Sheriff]] role, and another player is given the Murderer role. However, if there are only two players in a server, the Innocent role is excluded. Each role has specific objectives to achieve before the round ends. Listed below are the objectives of each role. 
[[File:Murderer.PNG|thumb|133x133px|A player receiving the [[Murderer]] role|alt=]]
[[Innocent|INNOCENTS]]: Evade the Murderer. Use your detective skills to expose the Murderer. You spawn without a [[Weapons|Weapon]].

[[Sheriff|SHERIFF]]: Assist the Innocents; you are the only one with a [[Weapons|Weapon]] who is capable of shooting the Murderer. You spawn with a [[:Category:Guns|Gun]].

[[Murderer|MURDERER]]: Eliminate everyone in the server and avoid getting shot by the Sheriff. You spawn with a [[:Category:Knives|Knife]].

[[Hero|HERO:]] Hero is only obtained after claiming the [[:Category:Guns|Gun]] once the Sheriff has died and then proceeding to shoot the Murderer with it.  You spawn without a [[Weapons|Weapon]] then claim a [[:Category:Guns|Gun]] over the remains of the previous Sheriff or Innocent’s body.

===<u>Rounds</u>===
{{See also|List of Links=[[Round Ending Screen]]}} 

[[File:Loading Map.png|thumb|220x220px|The text "Loading Map..." that appears at the top of a screen before a round starts.|alt=]]
Rounds are started when there is more than one player in a public server. Lobby mode can be enabled in [[Private Servers]] to disable rounds. Before a round, players must vote between three randomly selected maps, and the map with the most votes will be chosen. If there are no votes, one of the three maps will randomly be chosen. During a round, the mechanics of the chosen gamemode will be implemented. Rounds end when the Murderer or Assassins run out of time (all modes), the Murderer dies (Standard and Disguises), when there is one Assassin left (Assassin only), or the Murderer has eliminated everyone (Standard and Disguises).

===<u>Maps</u>===
{{Dedicated Page|Link=[[Maps]]}}

Throughout the history of Murder Mystery as a whole, [[:Category:Maps|Maps]] have been an integral part of the game, allowing for locations for rounds to take place in. Majority of the maps in Murder Mystery 2 were designed by [[Zyleak]] and [[Thexz]], and all these maps include secret hiding spots and hidden easter eggs. In the [[Lobby]], players may enter the voting room to vote between three randomly selected maps. If no player votes, a random map will be chosen. 
[[File:VotingRoom.png|thumb|220x220px|The Voting Room in the lobby.|alt=]]
As of now, there are currently twelve active maps. The following maps below are the playable maps:

